  "sourceAnatomyObservations": [
    "Native foot detail and direct192samples show a leftward branch/hook arising separately from each ankle/foot base and a rightward emerging group of long curved digits. Those visible directions exist in the image, rather than being created by mask names. They are consistent with a rearhallux/forwarddigit hypothesis; this is not certification of everydigitidentity or3Dopposition.",
    "For the screen-left foot, the leftward branch lies roughly x96..106,y144..152 and the forwardcurves x106..120,y147..161. The screen-right foot has a corresponding leftward branch around x114..124,y142..150 and forwardcurves x124..140,y144..159. These broad ranges are manual image observations with at least2outputpixel uncertainty; near/far are screen labels, not calibrated depth.",
    "Three forward curved rails are most evident at native scale, with distal overlap at192and uncertain exacttoe ownership. The original held reference also has a leftwardhook. Therefore this redraw must not be described as proof that a missinghallux was newly solved solely because a rear-region label exists.",
    "The source still depicts claws without an actual support raster between/behind them. Curved hooks and a plausible opposing branch do not demonstrate toes bearing around a particularcylinder, contactpressure or physicalgrip. Current support fit is blocked by missing input, not resolved by alpha or the staticpicture.",
    "Broad body/head/bill/tail proportions are coherent with the conditioning perched-source study. Both controls share the same unchanged185.885world extent and alpha128bbox6,40,178,160. UpperbodyRGBA differs at7499pixels; no fixedbodypromise was made and no universal pixel-equality or bbox acceptance gate is applied.",
    "This comparison is between two staticart studies, not a temporal old\u2192newaction join. Neither replaces the useful groundneutral nor establishes perching/takeoff/landing animation."
  ],
